WEBVTT

00:00:29.039 --> 00:00:31.789
So how can you figure out what’s a
genuine health concern

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:33.769
or a truly promising remedy,

00:00:33.769 --> 00:00:36.169
and what’s less conclusive?

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:36.949
In medicine,

00:00:36.949 --> 00:00:39.929
there’s often a disconnect between 
news headlines

00:00:39.929 --> 00:00:42.459
and the scientific research they cover.

00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:45.499
That’s because a headline is designed 
to catch attention—

00:00:45.499 --> 00:00:48.379
it’s most effective when 
it makes a big claim.

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:49.559
By contrast,

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:52.409
many scientific studies produce 
meaningful results

00:00:52.409 --> 00:00:55.909
when they focus on a narrow, 
specific question.

00:00:55.909 --> 00:00:57.899
The best way to bridge this gap

00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:02.239
is to look at the original research 
behind a headline.